     The bug cited down-thread explains why the statue
itself has the wrong weight; the special level loading
code created a random statue and then changed its monster
type without updating its weight to match the specified
type.  Whenever an object is put into a container, if it
is a statue or another container then it gets re-weighed
rather than use the weight attached to the object.  So
putting that statue into the bag caused the bag to add
the weight of a dwarf king instead of a newt or whatever.
But it didn't correct the statue's own weight in the
process, so when you took the statue back out, its
no-longer-correct weight assigned to it during item
creation came back into use for your inventory.

     The fix for fully updating a statue or corpse when
changing its type will have indirectly solved this too.
The weight during container manipulation will be the same
as the weight assigned to the objects involved.



